---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const faqData = [
  {
    question: "What are 'Pulses'?",
    answer: `"Pulses" are the credits used for content generation. The cost is split into two parts: a one-time Extraction fee and a per-network Generation fee. Extraction costs 1 pulse for articles and 1 pulse for media (video/audio). Generation costs 1 pulse per selected network. For example, a video for 3 networks costs 4 pulses (1 for extraction + 3 for generation).`,
  },
  {
    question: "How do Plans and Payments work?",
    answer: `We offer a Freemium model. The Free Plan includes 70 pulses monthly. Paid Plans (Classic & Pro) are a one-time payment for 30 days of access and a larger pulse package. You can also buy extra non-expiring Pulse Packs anytime.`,
  },
  {
    question: "My post failed. Did I lose my Pulse?",
    answer: `It depends on when the failure occurs. Pulses for **Extraction** (reading an article or processing media) and **Generation** (creating content with AI) are consumed as soon as those actions are successfully completed, which happens *before* you click "Publish". If content generation succeeds, those pulses are used, even if a later publication attempt fails. We do not have a separate charge for the act of publishing itself.`,
  },
  {
    question: "What is your refund policy?",
    answer: `All purchases of subscription plans and Pulse Packs are final and non-refundable. We encourage you to use the Free Plan to evaluate the service before making a purchase.`,
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Referral Program work?",
    answer: `You can find your unique referral link in your Account Settings. When a new user signs up using your link and makes their first purchase, you will automatically receive a bonus of 100 pulses.`,
  },
  {
    question: "What if article scraping from a URL fails?",
    answer: `If scraping fails during the extraction step, your pulse will not be used. You can then switch to the "Pulsar from Text" mode on the dashboard to paste the article content directly, bypassing the scraping step.`,
  },
  {
    question: "What are the media/character limits for each social network?",
    answer: `Each network has different limits. For example, Instagram & Threads support carousels up to 10 items, while LinkedIn and X (Twitter) do not. File size limits also vary. The character counter in the app helps you stay within each network's text limits.`,
  },
  {
    question: "How do I get credentials for Telegram?",
    answer: `You need a Bot Token from @BotFather and a Channel/Chat ID. To get the ID, add your bot to the channel and forward a message from it to @userinfobot.`,
  },
  {
    question: "How do I get the Webhook URL for Discord?",
    answer: `In your Discord server, go to Server Settings > Integrations and click "Create Webhook". Copy the generated URL and paste it into the Connections page on PostPulsar.`,
  },
  {
    question: "I generated content and refreshed the page. Did I lose my work?",
    answer: `No. The last content you generated is automatically saved in your browser. If you refresh the page, the content will be reloaded on the dashboard.`,
  },
  {
    question: "Do you store my credit card information?",
    answer: `No. All payment processing is handled securely by Stripe. We never see or store your credit card details.`,
  },
  {
    question: "Why can't I post videos?",
    answer: `Video publishing is a feature of our Pro plan. The Free and Basic plans support text and image posts. To unlock video publishing, please consider upgrading to Pro.`,
  },
  {
    question: "Why is PostPulsar asking me to reconnect a social network?",
    answer: `For your security, access permissions expire periodically. When they do, we ask you to re-authenticate to securely renew the permission. Your data and settings are safe.`,
  },
  {
    question: "Why does video upload to some networks take longer?",
    answer: `To ensure compatibility, videos for stricter networks like Instagram and LinkedIn go through a quick optimization process. This increases the success rate of the publication and may take a few moments.`,
  },
  {
    question: "I got an error when posting to X (Twitter). What happened?",
    answer: `X (Twitter) has a strict anti-spam policy. If you try to post the same or very similar text multiple times, it may be blocked. Try making a small change to the content and posting again.`,
  },
  {
    question: "Why can't I connect my Instagram account?",
    answer: `To connect, your Instagram account must be a Professional Account (Business or Creator) and it must be linked to a Facebook Page. Personal accounts are not supported.`,
  },
  {
    question: "Why can't I post to a LinkedIn Company Page?",
    answer: `Currently, our LinkedIn integration only supports posting to Personal Profiles. We plan to support Company Pages in a future update.`,
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqData.map((item) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: item.question,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      "@type": "Answer",
      text: item.answer,
    },
  })),
};
---

<Layout title="FAQ - PostPulsar">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 md:px-6 py-12 max-w-4xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold uppercase text-center mb-8">
      // Frequently Asked Questions
    </h1>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          What are "Pulses"?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            "Pulses" are the credits you use to generate content in PostPulsar.
            The cost of an action is divided into two parts to make it more
            efficient and fair:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>
              <strong>Extraction Cost (one-time fee):</strong> This is paid once
              per "Pulsar" action for reading the source content.
              <ul class="list-['-_'] list-inside ml-4">
                <li><strong>1 Pulse</strong> to read an article from a URL.</li>
                <li>
                  <strong>1 Pulse</strong> for a media file (video/audio)
                  from a URL.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Generation Cost:</strong> This is paid for each social network
              you select.
              <ul class="list-['-_'] list-inside ml-4">
                <li><strong>1 Pulse</strong> per network.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">
            This model ensures you only pay for expensive tasks once, even if you generate content for many networks.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            <strong>Example:</strong> Generating content for <strong
              >3 networks</strong
            > from a <strong>video URL</strong> costs <strong>4 pulses</strong> (1
            for extraction + 3 for generation).
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          How do Plans and Payments work?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            We offer a Freemium model with several options to fit your needs:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Free Plan:</strong> Get started with a monthly allowance of
              <strong>70 pulses</strong> to explore the core features.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Paid Plans (Classic & Pro):</strong> A plan purchase is a <strong
                >one-time payment</strong
              > that grants you <strong>30 days of access</strong> to the plan's
              features and its corresponding pulse package (210 for Classic, 500
              for Pro). It is <strong>not a recurring subscription</strong>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Pulse Packs:</strong> Need a temporary boost? You can buy extra
              pulse packs at any time. These pulses are added to your account and
              do not expire.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">
            You can purchase or renew a plan on the <a
              href="/app/billing"
              class="text-primary hover:underline">Billing</a
            > page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          My post failed. Did I lose my Pulse?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            It depends on when the failure occurs. Pulses for <strong
              >Extraction</strong
            > (reading an article or transcribing media) and <strong
              >Generation</strong
            > (creating content with AI) are consumed as soon as those actions are
            successfully completed.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            These actions happen *before* you click "Publish". Therefore, if
            content generation succeeds, those pulses are used, even if a later
            publication attempt fails.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We do not have a separate charge for the act of publishing itself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          What is your refund policy?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            All purchases of subscription plans and Pulse Packs are final and
            non-refundable. We do not offer refunds or credits for partially
            used periods or unused pulses.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We encourage you to use the Free Plan to evaluate the service before
            making a purchase. For more details, please see our <a
              href="/terms"
              class="text-primary hover:underline">Terms of Service</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          How does the Referral Program work?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            Yes, we do! You can earn bonus pulses by inviting other creators to
            join PostPulsar.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            You can find your unique referral link in your <a
              href="/app/settings"
              class="text-primary hover:underline">Account Settings</a
            > page. Share this link with your friends and colleagues.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            When a new user signs up using your link and makes their first
            purchase (either a subscription plan or a pulse pack), you will
            automatically receive a bonus of <strong>100 pulses</strong> as our thank
            you! You can track your successful referrals on the same settings page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          What if article scraping from a URL fails?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            If scraping fails during the extraction step, your pulse will not be
            used. You can then switch to the <strong>"Pulsar from Text"</strong>
            mode on the dashboard to paste the article content directly, bypassing
            the scraping step.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          What are the media/character limits for each social network?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            Each social network has its own rules for posts. Here’s a quick
            guide to what PostPulsar supports for each platform:
          </p>

          <h3 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
            Carousel Posts (Multiple Images/Videos)
          </h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li>
              <strong>Instagram & Threads:</strong> You can post a carousel with
              up to 10 items.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Discord:</strong> You can attach up to 10 files.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>LinkedIn, X (Twitter), Facebook, & Telegram:</strong> Do not
              support carousel posts. You can attach one image or one video.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">Media File Size Limits</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li>
              <strong>Instagram, Threads, LinkedIn, X, Facebook:</strong> Images
              up to 2MB and videos up to 200MB.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Telegram:</strong> Up to 50MB per file.</li>
            <li><strong>Discord:</strong> Up to 8MB per file.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">About the Character Counter</h3>
          <p>
            The character counter you see for networks like X (Twitter) and
            Threads is there to help you. Each social media platform has a
            maximum length for posts. The counter shows how many characters you
            have left. If it shows a negative number, your post is too long and
            you need to shorten it before publishing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details
        id="telegram-credentials"
        class="group border border-border/50 p-6"
      >
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          How do I get credentials for Telegram?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            To connect to Telegram, you need a <strong>Bot Token</strong> and a <strong
              >Channel/Chat ID</strong
            >.
          </p>
          <ol class="list-decimal list-inside mt-2 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Bot Token:</strong> Talk to the <a
                href="https://t.me/BotFather"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="text-primary hover:underline">BotFather</a
              > on Telegram, create a new bot, and it will provide you with the token.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Channel/Chat ID:</strong>
              <ul class="list-disc list-inside ml-4 mt-1">
                <li>
                  Add your bot as an administrator to your channel or group.
                </li>
                <li>Send any message to the channel/group.</li>
                <li>
                  Forward that message to the <a
                    href="https://t.me/userinfobot"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="text-primary hover:underline">@userinfobot</a
                  > bot. It will reply with the channel/chat ID.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Copy and paste these two pieces of information into the
            corresponding fields on the <a
              href="/app/connections"
              class="text-primary hover:underline">Connections</a
            > page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details
        id="discord-credentials"
        class="group border border-border/50 p-6"
      >
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          How do I get the Webhook URL for Discord?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>To post to a Discord channel, you need a Webhook URL.</p>
          <ol class="list-decimal list-inside mt-2 space-y-2">
            <li>
              In your Discord server, go to <strong
                >Server Settings > Integrations</strong
              >.
            </li>
            <li>Click on <strong>"Create Webhook"</strong>.</li>
            <li>
              Give the webhook a name, choose the channel where it will post,
              and click <strong>"Copy Webhook URL"</strong>.
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Paste this URL into the corresponding field on the <a
              href="/app/connections"
              class="text-primary hover:underline">Connections</a
            > page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          I generated content and refreshed the page. Did I lose my work?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            No. To prevent losing work, the last content you generated is
            automatically saved in your browser. If you refresh the page, the
            content will be reloaded on the dashboard, ready for you to continue
            editing or to publish.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          Do you store my credit card information?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            No. We never store your credit card details. All payment processing
            is handled securely and directly by Stripe, one of the largest and
            most secure payment platforms in the world. We only receive
            confirmation that the payment was successful.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          Why can't I post videos?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            Video publishing is a feature of our <strong>Pro plan</strong>. The
            Free plan allows text posts (with an exception for Instagram, which
            requires an image), and our Basic plan supports images. To unlock
            video publishing and other advanced features, please consider
            upgrading to Pro on the
            <a href="/app/billing" class="text-primary hover:underline"
              >Billing</a
            >
            page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          Why is PostPulsar asking me to reconnect a social network?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            Don't worry. For your security, the access permissions you grant us
            to post on your behalf have an expiration date. When they expire, we
            simply ask you to re-authenticate to securely renew the permission.
            Your data and settings remain saved.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          Why does video upload to some networks take longer?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            To ensure maximum compatibility, videos sent to networks with
            stricter rules (like Instagram and LinkedIn) go through a quick
            analysis and optimization process in our system. This ensures the
            file has the correct structure and dramatically increases the
            chances of a successful publication. This process may take a few
            moments.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          I got an error when posting to X (Twitter). What happened?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            X (Twitter) has a very strict anti-spam policy. If you try to post
            the same text (or very similar text) multiple times in a short
            period, the platform may block the publication. Please try making a
            small change to the content and posting again.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          Why can't I connect my Instagram account?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            To connect your Instagram account to PostPulsar, it must be a <strong
              >Professional Account (either Business or Creator)</strong
            >. Personal Instagram accounts cannot be connected.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Additionally, your Instagram Professional Account must be <strong
              >linked to a Facebook Page</strong
            >. During the authentication process, you will be asked to select
            the correct Instagram account and the associated Facebook Page.
            Please ensure you grant permissions for both.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-border/50 p-6">
        <summary
          class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center"
        >
          Why can't I post to a LinkedIn Company Page?
          <span
            class="transition-transform transform group-open:rotate-180 text-primary"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg
            >
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-foreground/70">
          <p>
            Currently, PostPulsar's integration with LinkedIn only supports
            posting to <strong>Personal Profiles</strong>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Publishing to Company Pages requires an additional verification step
            from LinkedIn which is not yet implemented in our system. We plan to
            support Company Pages in a future update.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

